%[text] # Getting Started with MATLAB®
%[text] The first thing you need to do to use this module is to open MATLAB. Option 2 is to work with these files on your local computer, and Option 1 is to access these files using MATLAB Online.
%[text] ## Option 1:
%[text] You can open these files in [MATLAB Online](https://matlab.mathworks.com/open/github/v1?repo=MathWorks-Teaching-Resources/Biosciences-Working-With-Data&project=BiosciencesWorkingWithData.prj). You’ll need to login to your MathWorks account (if you are with a university, use your .edu email address to access your university’s license).
%[text] ## Option 2:
%[text] 1. If MATLAB isn't already installed on your computer, you'll need to do that first ([instructional video](https://www.mathworks.com/videos/install-matlab-on-personal-computers-campus-wide-license-1717472837232.html)).
%[text] 2. Download this repository to your computer. Unzip the folder. Then you can open the project in MATLAB by double-clicking `BiosciencesWorkingWithData.prj`. Alternately, in the folder on your computer you can click “Open with” and then MATLAB. You can also open MATLAB directly. The MATLAB editor will open and look like this: \
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![](text:image:6576)
%[text] The "Files" panel and its icon, outlined in orange, shows the contents of the folder you are currently working in. This is called your working directory. The full path to this directory, outlined in blue, is written out above the command window.
%[text] On the top left of the directory line, you can click "browse for a folder": ![](text:image:24ab) 
%[text] This opens a file picker where you can navigate through your computer to find the folder you want to work in (navigate to the repository folder for this module that you downloaded). You will want to save any data you access to this folder, and always make sure that you are working from that folder as you go through the module.
%[text] You can learn more about the desktop layout and options in the [documentation](https://www.mathworks.com/help/matlab/matlab_env/overview-of-new-desktop-layout.html).
%[text] ## Further information
%[text] If you want a little more information on how to work in MATLAB and what the other parts of the MATLAB window do, check out [Getting Started with MATLAB](https://www.mathworks.com/products/matlab/getting-started.html) or take the [MATLAB Onramp](https://matlabacademy.mathworks.com/details/matlab-onramp/gettingstarted).

